{title: All Glory, Laud, and Honor}
{artist: Theodulf of Orléans · tr. John Mason Neale}
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 92}

Chorus
[Bb]All glory, laud, and [F]honor to [Gm]thee, Re[F]deemer, [Bb]King,
to whom the lips of [F]children made [Gm]sweet ho[F]sannas [Bb]ring!

Verse 1
Thou [Bb]art the King of [F]Israel, thou [Gm]David's [F]royal [Bb]Son,
who in the Lord's name [F]comest, the [Gm]King and [F]blessed [Bb]one.

Verse 2
All glory, [Bb]laud and honor, To Thee, Redeemer, King, [F]To Whom the lips [Gm]of [F]children Made [Bb]sweet hosannas
ring. The company of angels Are praising Thee on [F]High, And mortal [Gm]men and all things [F]Created [Bb]make reply.

Verse 3
All glory, [Bb]laud and honor, To Thee, Redeemer, King, To [F]Whom the lips [Gm]of children [F]Made sweet [Bb]hosannas ring.
The people of the Hebrews With palms before Thee [F]went; Our prayer and [Gm]praise and anthems [F]Before Thee [Bb]we present.

Verse 4
All glory, [Bb]laud and honor, To Thee, Redeemer, King, To [F]Whom the lips [Gm]of children [F]Made sweet [Bb]hosannas ring.
To Thee, before Thy passion, They sang their hymns [F]of praise; To Thee, [Gm]now high exalted, [F]Our melody [Bb]we raise.

Verse 5
All glory, [Bb]laud and honor, To Thee, Redeemer, King, To [F]Whom the lips [Gm]of children [F]Made sweet [Bb]hosannas ring.
Thou didst accept their praises; Accept the prayers we [F]bring, Who in all [Gm]good delightest, Thou [F]good and [Bb]gracious King.
